        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the I'3ace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be holden at the COURT HOUSE, KNUISFORD, in and tor the said County, On MONDAY, the 19th day of October next. at Eleven o'clock in the Foienoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Anneals arising within the Hundreds of Bucklow, Maccicsfild and Northwich, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners com- mitted from such Hundreds, will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Patty Juries for the Knuts- ford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 19th day of October, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. TEE COURT will be Adjourned to the Castle of Chester, on WEDNESDAY, the 21st day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when another Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals *rising within the Hundreds of Rroxron, Eddisburv. Nantwich, and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last- mentioned Hundreds will take place at such adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at tile opening of the Court on EDNESDAY,thO 21st day of October next, at Elevcn o'clock in the' Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Che.tar, 28th Seetorrb.r. 1903.</p>
